empts RemoveAll on the temporary directory; cleanup error supersedes the original error.","Metadata or rename error returns without further cleanup.","Parent-directory open or Sync failure returns after rename has succeeded.","Reaping failure returns after publication and may follow partial deletion.","finalize can return before closing the state handle if Flush or Sync fails."],"async_boundaries":["Filesystem visibility begins at rename before later Close steps complete."],"produces_fact_ids":["file_snapshot_rename_completed"],"consumes_fact_ids":[],"cross_activity_effects":{},"existing_protections":["Flush and enabled state Sync precede final metadata writing.","Final metadata writing precedes rename.","Enabled non-Windows parent-directory Sync precedes automatic reaping."],"source_ids":["file_snapshot.go:397:551"],"unknowns":["Crash durability depends on filesystem and platform semantics not supplied here.","The caller's interpretation of errors after rename is unread.","Automatic retention can remove the newly published snapshot if it ranks outside the retained prefix."]},{"id":"file_snapshot_terminal_repeat","primary_activity":"A6","execution_owner":"Caller executing Close or Cancel after closed has been set","protocol_context":"Sink with closed == true","trigger":"A repeated or alternate terminal call observes closed.","legal_preconditions":[],"implementation_guards":["Return nil immediately when closed is true."],"reads":["closed"],"writes":[],"durable_effects":[],"external_effects":["Returns nil without retrying finalization, metadata writing, publication, reaping or cleanup."],"important_branches":["The same result follows an earlier successful or failed Close or Cancel."],"async_boundaries":[],"produces_fact_ids":[],"consumes_fact_ids":[],"cross_activity_effects":{},"existing_protections":["Avoids repeating terminal processing once the flag is set."],"source_ids":["file_snapshot.go:397:551"],"unknowns":["Nil from this branch establishes no new publication 