List returns at most retain entries sorted descending by term, index and then ID.","Directory scan error is returned; per-directory metadata problems are logged and skipped."],"important_branches":["Discovery does not read state.bin or validate CRC.","Decoded metadata ID is not checked against the directory name."],"async_boundaries":["Directory scanning and metadata reads do not provide a demonstrated atomic view."],"produces_fact_ids":["file_snapshot_metadata_eligible"],"consumes_fact_ids":[],"cross_activity_effects":{},"existing_protections":["Temporary-directory exclusion","Metadata decoding and supported-version filters"],"source_ids":["file_snapshot.go:160:396","file_snapshot.go:397:551"],"unknowns":["The numeric supported version bounds are defined outside the supplied file.","Eligibility does not establish state readability or successful FSM restoration."]},{"id":"file_snapshot_open","primary_activity":"A6","execution_owner":"Caller executing FileSnapshotStore.Open","protocol_context":"Caller-supplied snapshot ID","trigger":"Open is called.","legal_preconditions":["Allowed ID provenance and concurrent filesystem mutation are unresolved."],"implementation_guards":["Require metadata decoding and state-file opening.","Read the entire state file and compare computed CRC64 against metadata CRC.","Require successful rewind before returning a reader."],"reads":["meta.json and state.bin under the supplied ID"],"writes":["Read handle offset and in-memory checksum"],"durable_effects":[],"external_effects":["Returns metadata and a buffered reader positioned at the beginning, or an error.","Closes the state handle on read, checksum or seek failure."],"important_branches":["Does not apply getSnapshots temporary-directory or supported-version filters.","Does not explicitly compare actual byte count with metadata Size or metadata ID with the requested ID."],"async_boundaries":["The caller consumes the returned reader after checksum verification has completed."],"produces_fact_ids":["file_snapshot_open_crc_validated"],"consumes_fact_ids":[],"cross_activity_effects":{},"existing_protections":["Full-file CRC comparison before returning the reader","Rewind before caller consumption"],"source_ids":["file_snapshot.go:1:159","file_snapshot.go:160:396"],"unknowns":["CRC agreement does not establish semantic consistency with index, term, configuration or FSM state.","Protection against mutation between validation and subsequent reads is not shown.","Actual recovery and transfer consumers are unread."]},{"id":"file_snapshot_reap","primary_activity":"A6","execution_owner":"Caller executing FileSnapshotStore.ReapSnapshots directly or through Close","protocol_context":"Eligible metadata from one getSnapshots invocation","trigger":"Explicit reclamation or successful preceding Close publication steps","legal_preconditions":[],"implementation_guards":["Return on discovery error.","Select only entries beyond the retain prefix."],"reads":["Descending metadata ordering, retain and each selected metadata ID"],"writes":["Removes paths formed from the store path and selected metadata IDs."],"durable_effects":["RemoveAll deletes selected snapshot artifacts; earlier deletions are not rolled back after a later error.","No explicit directory Sync follows these deletions."],"external_effects":["Returns the first removal error or nil."],"important_branches":["Selection relies on metadata eligibility without opening or CRC-validating retained state files.","Removal paths use metadata IDs rather than preserved directory-entry names.","Skipped temporary or unreadable-metadata directories are outside this reclamation set."],"async_boundaries":["Enumeration and sequential removals are separate filesystem operations."],"produces_fact_ids":[],"consumes_fact_ids":["file_snapshot_metadata_eligible"],"cross_activity_effects":{},"existing_protections":["Public constructors require retaining at least one entry.","Reclamation keeps the highest-ranked eligible metadata prefi