idate.","A nonempty list whose attempts all return false produces an error."],"async_boundaries":[],"produces_fact_ids":[],"consumes_fact_ids":["file_snapshot_metadata_eligible","startup_snapshot_restore_helper_returned","startup_snapshot_restore_bypassed"],"cross_activity_effects":{"A4":"Installs committed and latest configuration values from the accepted listed candidate after explicit metadata selection or successful legacy peer decoding.","A5":"Sets LastApplied to the accepted listed candidate's Index, including when restoration was explicitly bypassed.","A6":"Sets LastSnapshot coordinates from the accepted listed candidate."},"existing_protections":["Open or restoration-helper failure does not itself cause candidate coordinate installation.","Fallback attempts another candidate in the returned list.","Failure to restore every candidate in a nonempty list is surfaced as an error."],"source_ids":["api.go:600:760","file_snapshot.go:160:396"],"unknowns":["The metadata-eligibility consumption edge applies only when FileSnapshotStore is selected; activation is not established.","The two attempt-result facts are alternative branch inputs, not jointly required facts.","The retained-prefix contract remains unresolved; fallback does not establish that any listed candidate can be restored.","Setter internals and any downstream replay behavior are not established by the attached source."]},{"id":"startup_snapshot_restore_attempt","primary_activity":"A3","execution_owner":"Initialization caller executing the normal branch of Raft.tryRestoreSingleSnapshot","protocol_context":"One listed SnapshotMeta with NoSnapshotRestoreOnStart false","trigger":"restoreSnapshot attempts a listed candidate.","legal_preconditions":["Called within initialization-owned snapshot selection."],"implementation_guards":["Return false when SnapshotStore.Open returns an error.","Return false when fsmRestoreAndMeasure returns an error.","Return true only after both calls return without error."],"reads":["NoSnapshotRestoreOnStart","Listed snapshot ID and Size","Reader returned by the selected SnapshotStore.Open"],"writes":["Passes r.fsm and the opened source to fsmRestoreAndMeasure; actual FSM mutations are unresolved."],"durable_effects":[],"external_effects":["Calls SnapshotStore.Open using the listed snapshot ID.","Calls fsmRestoreAndMeasure using the listed Size.","Closes the source after either helper success or helper failure; Close errors are ignored.","Returns a boolean attempt result."],"important_branches":["Open failure prevents invocation of the restoration helper.","Restoration-helper failure closes the source and permits the outer selector to attempt another candidate.","Metadata returned by Open is discarded; subsequent outer updates use the original listed metadata.","When FileSnapshotStore is selected, successful Open supplies a reader whose previously observed bytes passed CRC validation."],"async_boundaries":["Restoration consumes the returned reader after Open validation; no immutability guarantee is established."],"produces_fact_ids":["startup_snapshot_restore_helper_returned"],"consumes_fact_ids":["file_snapshot_open_crc_validated"],"cross_activity_effects":{},"existing_protections":["Open failure and restoration-helper failure remain distinguishable from successful attempt completion.","The opened source is closed on both helper-result branches."],"source_ids":["api.go:600:760","file_snapshot.go:160:396"],"unknowns":["The checksum fact consumption edge is conditional on selection of FileSnapshotStore.","The restoration helper's implementation and any partial FSM mutation after failure are unread.","No comparison between listed metadata and Open-returned metadata is shown.","Concurrent mutation between listing, opening and restoring remains unresolved."]},{"id":"startup_snapshot_restore_bypass","primary_activity":"A3","execution_owner":"Initialization caller executing the bypass branch of Raft.tryRestoreSingleSnapshot","protocol_context":"One