ing returned nil and the temporary directory was renamed to the suffix-stripped path. This does not assert successful completion of the remaining Close steps.","identity":{"snapshot":"Store path, sink metadata ID and this construction attempt","establishment":"Successful os.Rename within the first Close"},"established_by":["file_snapshot_close_first"],"consumed_by":[],"validity_context":"An observation at the rename point, before optional parent-directory Sync and retention reclamation; does not assert continuing file existence.","representation":["Successful Rename result","Final-path directory containing finalized state and metadata under the observed operation sequence"],"invalidators":[],"reinterpreters":[],"durability":"File Sync is conditional on noSync; parent-directory synchronization occurs later and is skipped on Windows. Rename success alone is not a crash-recovery guarantee.","recovery":"getSnapshots can discover final-path metadata after restart; Open performs separate state validation. Actual restart orchestration is unread.","source_ids":["file_snapshot.go:397:551"],"unknowns":["Later parent synchronization or reclamation can fail while this historical rename observation remains true.","ReapSnapshots can subsequently remove this path, including during the same Close.","This fact has no explicit consumer edge because discovery does not verify this construction history."]},{"id":"file_snapshot_metadata_eligible","meaning":"During one discovery invocation, a non-temporary directory yielded decodable metadata with a supported version and was admitted to the metadata ordering. State-file readability and integrity have not been established.","identity":{"discovery":"Store path and getSnapshots invocation","entry":"Scanned directory name and decoded metadata, including its independently supplied ID"},"established_by":["file_snapshot_discover"],"consumed_by":["file_snapshot_reap","startup_snapshot_select"],"validity_context":"Historical eligibility within thi